        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "97de96ee-12b9-5d44-9440-2c5639e99963",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Countries: Russia, United Kingdom\n- Events: World War I, World War II, Cold War, Russian Revolution, February Revolution\n- People: Nicholas II\n- Governments: Russian Empire, Provisional Government\n\nFacts:\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies in World War I, but their relations were strained by the Russian Revolution of 1917.\n- In the first revolution of February 1917, dated March 1917 in the Gregorian calendar, Emperor Nicholas II abdicated and the Russian Empire collapsed.\n- During the February 1917 revolution, the old Russian regime was replaced by a Provisional Government.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were allies again in World War II.\n- Russia and the United Kingdom were in hostile opposition during the Cold War from 1947 to 1991.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
